# Check the bottom of Server Maintenance after every change

`ServerMaintenanceView` (in `SettingsView.swift`) has repeatedly ended up with its bottom clipped
after edits. Whenever it changes, look at it in the simulator before saying the work is done, and
show the screenshot.

1. Temporarily present it the way the app does, in a sheet, and scroll to the true end of the form:
   - in `PoolStatusApp.swift`, add to `StatusView()` a `.sheet(isPresented: .constant(true))` holding
     `NavigationStack { ScrollViewReader { proxy in ServerMaintenanceView().task { sleep ~8s;
     proxy.scrollTo("bottom", anchor: .bottom) } } }.environment(store)`
   - as the last thing in the view's `Form`, add
     `Color.clear.frame(height: 1).listRowBackground(Color.clear).id("bottom")`
   - mark every temporary line `// TEMP-HARNESS`
2. Build, install, launch and screenshot (simulator "iPhone 17 Pro", A1C3AA84-…):
   `xcodebuild -project PoolStatus.xcodeproj -scheme PoolStatus -destination 'generic/platform=iOS Simulator' -derivedDataPath /tmp/PoolStatusDD build`,
   then `xcrun simctl install`, `xcrun simctl launch --terminate-running-process`, wait, and
   `xcrun simctl io <udid> screenshot`.
3. The Factory Reset footer must be fully visible above the home indicator. Also check with the
   software keyboard after focusing a text field (`defaults write com.apple.iphonesimulator
   ConnectHardwareKeyboard -bool false`, relaunch Simulator, reboot the device; delete the default
   afterwards) and at a large text size (`xcrun simctl ui <udid> content_size accessibility-large`,
   then back to `large`).
4. Remove the harness (`rg TEMP ios/PoolStatus/PoolStatus` finds nothing), rebuild and reinstall
   the real app.
